---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import analytics from '../../assets/dvzz-analytics.png';

// Orders per day, counted from the store's order export (aggregated, no customer data).
const firstDrop = { start: 'Jun 25, 2021', end: 'Jul 4', orders: [1, 0, 0, 40, 4, 3, 1, 4, 2, 1] };
const secondDrop = { start: 'Feb 2, 2022', end: 'Feb 11', orders: [4, 1, 15, 3, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0] };
const peak = Math.max(...firstDrop.orders, ...secondDrop.orders);
---

<Base
  title="DvzzPins · David Salazar"
  description="I ran DvzzPins, a Shopify pin store. Each drop drew a rush of orders: 40 in a single day, customers in 24 states, and designs that sold out completely."
  current="work"
>
  <div class="case">
    <header class="case-head">
      <div class="col">
        <h1 data-reveal>DvzzPins</h1>
        <p class="lede" data-reveal>
          A Shopify pin store I ran on my own. Every drop drew a rush: 40 orders in a single day,
          and four designs that sold out completely.
        </p>
        <dl class="spec" data-reveal>
          <dt>What</dt>
          <dd>An online store selling enamel pins in limited drops, December 2020 to October 2022.</dd>
          <dt>Role</dt>
          <dd>Founder and only operator: product development, designers, suppliers, inventory, launches and customer messages.</dd>
          <dt>Tools</dt>
          <dd>Shopify, including its analytics and order exports.</dd>
          <dt>Numbers</dt>
          <dd>199 orders and 258 items to 156 customers in 24 US states. $3,760 in net sales.</dd>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section>
      <div class="col">
        <h2 data-reveal>What I did</h2>
        <div class="runin">
          <p data-reveal>
            <strong>Product development.</strong> I turned concepts into products with designers
            and manufacturers. Each design went through a supplier proof that fixed the size,
            quantity, enamel and plating type and color codes, and that carried a warning: any
            change after the printing plates are made means a new setup or mold charge. That made
            proof review the step where mistakes were cheapest to catch.
          </p>
          <p data-reveal>
            <strong>Suppliers.</strong> I worked through specs and proofs with supplier GS-JJ,
            negotiated a $50 credit on a repeat mold charge, and got quotes for a charm line.
          </p>
          <p data-reveal>
            <strong>Running the drops.</strong> I managed inventory, planned each launch and
            answered customers, and used the store's data to see what sold and when.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="band">
      <div class="col">
        <h2 data-reveal>How the drops went</h2>
        <p data-reveal>
          The first drop landed on June 28, 2021. The store took 40 orders that day, a fifth of
          every order it would ever receive, and 48 in its first six days.
        </p>
        <div data-reveal>
          <div class="columns-chart" role="img" aria-label={`Orders per day from ${firstDrop.start} to ${firstDrop.end}: ${firstDrop.orders.join(', ')}`}>
            {firstDrop.orders.map((n) => (
              <span style={`height:${(n / peak) * 100}%`}>{n >= 10 && <em>{n}</em>}</span>
            ))}
          </div>
          <div class="columns-labels" aria-hidden="true"><span>{firstDrop.start}</span><span>{firstDrop.end}</span></div>
          <p class="figure-note">Orders per day, first drop.</p>
        </div>
        <p data-reveal>
          The next drops did the same. August 2021 brought 70 orders, with 19 on August 3 and 14 on
          August 22. In February 2022, 15 orders came on a single day, and 23 of that month's 25
          arrived in the first four days.
        </p>
        <div data-reveal>
          <div class="columns-chart" role="img" aria-label={`Orders per day from ${secondDrop.start} to ${secondDrop.end}: ${secondDrop.orders.join(', ')}`}>
            {secondDrop.orders.map((n) => (
              <span style={`height:${(n / peak) * 100}%`}>{n >= 10 && <em>{n}</em>}</span>
            ))}
          </div>
          <div class="columns-labels" aria-hidden="true"><span>{secondDrop.start}</span><span>{secondDrop.end}</span></div>
          <p class="figure-note">Orders per day, February 2022 drop.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="col">
        <h2 data-reveal>Who showed up</h2>
        <ul data-reveal>
          <li>156 customers in 24 US states, plus one order to Canada.</li>
          <li>29 of those customers ordered more than once, and one ordered five times.</li>
          <li>Four designs sold out completely, and 86.6% of products sold through overall.</li>
          <li>Three products made up about 76% of the 258 items sold, across 11 products in total.</li>
          <li>4,959 store sessions, with an average order value of $18.32.</li>
        </ul>
        <p data-reveal>
          Most visitors arrived directly (about 73%) or from social media (about 20%), and only
          about 3% came from search. That points to word of mouth and sharing around each drop, not
          people searching for pins.
        </p>
        <figure class="wide-shot" data-reveal style="margin:1.5rem 0">
          <Image
            src={analytics}
            alt="Shopify analytics for 2021 to 2022: total sales of $4,481, 199 orders and 4,959 store sessions, each with two large peaks in mid 2021 and a smaller one in early 2022"
            widths={[640, 1000, 1400]}
            sizes="(min-width: 40rem) 35rem, 92vw"
          />
          <figcaption class="figure-note">
            Shopify analytics, January 2021 to December 2022. Each peak is a drop. Total sales
            include shipping, so they are higher than net sales.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="band">
      <div class="col">
        <h2 data-reveal>How it ended</h2>
        <p data-reveal>
          Orders tapered off after the February 2022 drop, and I closed the business in October
          2022.
        </p>
        <div class="actions" data-reveal>
          <a class="btn" href="/#work">Back to work</a>
          <a class="textlink" href="/#contact">Get in touch</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
